<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n76000" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐρίζω</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιῶ, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὖρος</span> A) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>carry
				with a fair wind, waft on the way</i>, of words and prayers,
				<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				317
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ ὀρθὸν οὐ.</span>
			<i>speed on the way, guide prosperously</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				695
			</span></i> (lyr.): an acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτούς</span> may
			be supplied in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				602
			</span></i> (but Sch. took it intr. 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐριοδρομεῖν</span>
			).</div>
